<section class="values">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-header">
      <p class="section-header__eyebrow">Why Sockethub</p>
      <h2 class="section-header__title">Why Sockethub</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="values__grid">
      <article class="value-card">
        <div class="value-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/>
            <path d="M3 9 L12 14 L21 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="value-card__title">One format, every protocol</h3>
        <p>ActivityStreams 2.0 JSON in, ActivityStreams 2.0 JSON out. No protocol-specific code in your frontend.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="value-card">
        <div class="value-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="12" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/>
            <path d="M8 21 H16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M12 17 V21" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <circle cx="12" cy="11" r="2.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="value-card__title">Browser-safe, server-side state</h3>
        <p>Sockethub holds long-lived connections, session credentials, and reconnect logic. Your app stays thin.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="value-card">
        <div class="value-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/>
            <path d="M12 3 V7 M12 17 V21 M3 12 H7 M17 12 H21" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <path d="M5.6 5.6 L8.4 8.4 M15.6 15.6 L18.4 18.4 M5.6 18.4 L8.4 15.6 M15.6 8.4 L18.4 5.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="value-card__title">Pluggable platforms</h3>
        <p>Add support for new protocols by implementing a small platform interface. Your frontend never changes.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="code-peek">
  <div class="container code-peek__inner">
    <div class="code-peek__copy">
      <p class="section-header__eyebrow"><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/activitystreams-core/">ActivityStreams 2.0</a></p>
      <h2 class="code-peek__title">The same envelope for every protocol</h2>
      <p>
        Every message is a JSON-LD ActivityStreams 2.0 object. The
        <code>@context</code> array names the AS2 base, the Sockethub
        vocabulary, and the specific platform — swap the platform URL and the
        same call reaches a different network.
      </p>
      <a href="/about" class="button is-light">Read the full model</a>
    </div>
<pre class="code-peek__block"><code>{
  <span class="tok-key">"@context"</span>: [
    <span class="tok-str">"https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams"</span>,
    <span class="tok-str">"https://sockethub.org/ns/context/v1.jsonld"</span>,
    <span class="tok-str">"https://sockethub.org/ns/context/platform/xmpp/v1.jsonld"</span>
  ],
  <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>:   <span class="tok-str">"send"</span>,
